    "body": "## Merge order\n\n- **Merge this PR first.** Based on `main`.\n- #415, #418, #420 and #421 now contain this PR's commits (they follow `crossref` in tags, search, highlights and sync through the resolver defined here). After this merges, their diffs shrink to their own changes. Order: #437, #415, #418, #419, #420, #421.\n- **Overlap with the PDF page labels thread:** both change page logic in `sp-devonthink.org`. This PR leaves `sp-devonthink-first-page`, the offset options and the page parsing as #436 merged them; the resolver does not depend on how the page is computed.\n- #435 (store-link) is untouched here.\n\n## Why #436 missed insert-link\n\n- #436 added the crossref lookup inside `sp-devonthink-citar-open` (the `D` action) only.\n- `sp-devonthink-insert-link`, `sp-devonthink-open-from-note` and `sp-devonthink-set-keyword` each called `sp-reading-uuid` on the entry's own key, so an entry with only a crossref parent still failed with `No DEVONthink record named KEY.pdf`.\n- My #436 tests never went through the insert-link path.\n\n## Change\n\n- One shared resolver in the core module: `sp-devonthink-record KEY` returns `(:uuid U :supplier KEY-OR-PARENT :via PARENT-OR-NIL)`: own record first, then `crossref`, then `xref`. `sp-devonthink-resolve` (page logic from #436) builds on it.\n- `sp-devonthink-note-record-uuid [ACTION]` is the same decision for the current litnote: the `#+devonthink:` keyword, else the entry's record, else the parent's. When it uses the parent's record it says so in the echo area; with an `ACTION` it asks first (the action would reach the whole book).\n- `crossref` and `pages` are read with `citar-get-value`, then from `citar-get-entry` (case-insensitive) when that gives nothing.\n- Commands that now follow `crossref`:\n  - In this PR: `sp-devonthink-insert-link` (page prompt starts with the chapter's page plus offset), `sp-devonthink-open-from-note`, `sp-devonthink-set-keyword` (asks first), `sp-devonthink-citar-open`, and `sp-reading-open` (reading module, via `sp-devonthink-resolve` when loaded).\n  - In the stack (see Merge order): `sp-devonthink-tag-note` (#415, asks first), `sp-devonthink-similar-to-note` (#418, read-only, says which record), `sp-devonthink-highlights-import` (#420, asks first), and the sync report, backfill and field probe (#421; the backfill asks once before writing the parent's UUID into chapter notes, the probe asks first, the report lists \"Covered by the record of the crossref parent\").\n- Doc: \"Which record a citekey means\" in `sp-devonthink.org`. Tests: 31 in `sp-devonthink-test.el` (including the real interactive `insert-link` with an entry that has only a crossref parent) and 13 in `sp-reading-test.el`; the stack PRs add tests for their commands.\n\n## What was verified\n\n- [x] Unit tests, with citar and DEVONthink stubbed; tangle check passes on every branch.\n- [ ] Not verified: `citar-get-value` returning your `crossref` and `pages` fields, and real DEVONthink opens (no DEVONthink or your bibliography here).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Entry `incollection` with `crossref = {parent}` and `pages = {45--67}`; the parent has a PDF in DEVONthink, the entry does not.\n- [x] `M-x sp-devonthink-insert-link`, pick the entry: the echo area says `... is in PARENT: PDF page N ...`, the prompt starts with that page; Enter inserts `[[devonthink:PARENT-UUID::N][ENTRY p. N]]`; clicking opens the parent at page N.\n- [x] Clear the prompt, Enter: a link without a page.\n- [x] Litnote of the chapter (no `#+devonthink:`): `C-c k d o` opens the parent at the chapter's page.\n- [x] Same note, `C-c k d k`: asks about the parent's record; `n` writes nothing, `y` writes the parent's UUID.\n- [x] `D` in the citar Embark menu on the entry: opens the parent at the chapter's page.\n- [x] `M-x sp-reading-open` on the entry: same, with the message.\n- [ ] Entry with neither own record nor a parent record: `insert-link` says `No DEVONthink record named KEY.pdf, and no record for its crossref`.\n- [ ] If the crossref isn't found at all: `M-:` `(citar-get-value 'crossref \"KEY\")` and `(citar-get-entry \"KEY\")`, paste the output.\n- [ ] Stack commands (after merging them): on the chapter's note, `C-c k d t` (tags), `C-c k d a` (similar), `C-c k d h` (highlights), `M-x sp-devonthink-sync-report`, `sp-devonthink-sync-backfill`: each names the parent's record; the writing ones ask first and do nothing on `n`.\n\n## Revert guide\n\n- `git revert` the commits of this PR (three, newest first). If #415, #418, #420 or #421 merged already, revert their crossref commits first, since they call `sp-devonthink-note-record-uuid`.\n- Reverting restores the direct `sp-reading-uuid` lookups; `citar-open` keeps the #436 behaviour.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC",
